==Battleground==
*2 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore Jr.]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Berserkory]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**8 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Techn-Old Hyena]]s spawn, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
**3 [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jrs]] spawn, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Before the boss wave, make sure to build up your money.

Bring [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]], he is by far your best Wave Immune meatshield to deal with Berserkory. You'll be using [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to take advantage of Techn-Old Hyena's low DPH, since they will be repeatedly warped to safety. This eventually creates a giant stack of Octopus Cats which create a Wave Block mountain across the battlefield, and combined with [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]] for Bore Jr., ensures you're never without at least one on the field. As for damage, heavy hitters like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], or [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]] can be used to kill off the Bore Jrs. & Dogensteins & [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] works for the Berserkory. The Techn-Old Hyenas can either be bursted down via rushers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or dealt with using ranged units/ubers of your choosing.

